WEBVTT

00:00:26.252 --> 00:00:32.472
It's time to put Columbus on the stand
in History vs. Christopher Columbus.

00:00:32.472 --> 00:00:34.123
"Order, order in the court.

00:00:34.123 --> 00:00:36.614
Wait, am I even supposed to 
be at work today?"

00:00:36.614 --> 00:00:37.989
<i>Cough</i>

00:00:37.989 --> 00:00:39.380
"Yes, your Honor.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:43.910
From 1792, Columbus Day was celebrated
in many parts of the United States

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:47.245
on October 12th,
the actual anniversary date.

00:00:47.245 --> 00:00:51.170
But although it was declared
an official holiday in 1934,

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:54.783
individual states aren't required
to observe it.

00:00:54.783 --> 00:00:57.394
Only 23 states close public services,

00:00:57.394 --> 00:01:01.135
and more states are moving away
from it completely."